
b
;; This is a slightly more compact of "alternate-1.tur", using a single state and multiple
;; instructions per configuration to print a sequence of alternating 0's and 1's in
;; alternating squares. This is the second example given in Turing's "On Computable Numbers".
b null P:0 b
b 0 R R P:1 b
b 1 R R P:0 b
